From 7d78374d70c11effe454669e7cce672bcee74415 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:16:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: CI-run progress sweep follow-ups (woken card
 probes now, saturated runners, off-thread bounded sweep)

PR #1956 review nits (card t_01a1d3f39c27f68b), plus the PR #2040 review answers:

1. A card the sweep wakes is the immediate probe for runners-offline.<labels>:
   apply() appends PROBE_RELEASED_EVENT naming its asserting run (after_run), and
   shared_blocker_guard lets it spawn (_released_as_probe) until a later run of the
   card starts. probe_starts alone cannot tell a fresh release from a spent one: a
   card woken a second time for the same blocker already has its earlier runs (and
   the wake's synthesized run) there, so it was told it could run now but held for
   shared_blocker_probe_seconds (review 5889139629). Releases without after_run
   (probe_stranded_blockers, older rows) keep the probe_starts rule. A card woken
   while others already wait behind the blocker (filtered with _task_applies, as the
   guard does) is held with them, and its comment says for how long.
2. Saturated vs offline runners: when the repo (then org) actions/runners list is
   readable and an online runner carries the job's labels, the run is busy (park
   allowed, nothing woken). The org list is read only without an online repo match;
   its possible false busy (runner groups the repo cannot use) is documented.
   Otherwise every message says "no runner picked it up in 15 min".
3. The card scan runs in the sweep on the wake-check pool; submit_sweep does one
   indexed query on the dispatcher thread and starts a sweep only when a scheduled
   card's latest park is kind=ci (the sweep's own connection briefly takes the
   dispatch tick lock; a sweep every minute on every board made a concurrent
   dispatch_once skip). _LAST_CHECK is pruned to live CI waits per board.
4. A running sweep counts against the wake-check pool's MAX_CONCURRENT. One sweep
   reads at most MAX_CARDS_PER_SWEEP runs, least recently checked first, and starts
   no gh call after SWEEP_BUDGET_SECONDS, the runner-list reads included (a run cut
   off before its runner list is re-read first next sweep). confirm() documents its
   up-to-three 20 s gh calls on the park path.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_ci_progress.py covers each item; every added
condition has a killing mutant (27/27 + 5/5 earlier, 15/15 for the review answers;
the old spent rule fails the reviewer's repro test).
